# Sony DualSense Wireless Controller - Deadzone Reference
#
# This file is for reference only. Actual calibration is applied via udev rules
# in modules/gaming/gaming.nix using evdev-joystick.
#
# ==============================================================================
# Current Configuration (applied via udev on controller connect)
# ==============================================================================
#
# Left stick (movement): 2% deadzone
#   ABS_X: 1310 raw units (axis 0)
#   ABS_Y: 1310 raw units (axis 1)
#
# Right stick (camera):
#   ABS_RX: 1310 raw units (axis 2) - 2% horizontal
#   ABS_RY: 3276 raw units (axis 3) - 5% vertical (more drift prone)
#
# ==============================================================================
# Deadzone Reference Table
# ==============================================================================
#
# Percentage | Raw Value | Use Case
# ------------|-----------|--------------------------------
# 0%          | 0         | Raw input, fighting games
# 1%          | 655       | Maximum precision
# 2%          | 1310      | ✅ Current setting (movement/camera)
# 3%          | 1966      | Slightly more forgiving
# 5%          | 3276      | ✅ Current setting (vertical camera)
# 10%         | 6553      | Casual play, worn controllers
# 15%         | 9830      | SDL2 default, very worn controllers
#
# ==============================================================================
# Testing Commands
# ==============================================================================
#
# View current kernel calibration:
#   evdev-joystick --showcal /dev/input/by-id/usb-Sony_*-event-joystick
#
# Real-time axis testing:
#   evdev-joystick --test /dev/input/by-id/usb-Sony_*-event-joystick
#
# SDL2 controller testing:
#   sdl2-jstest --list
#   sdl2-jstest
#
# Re-apply udev rules (without replugging):
#   sudo udevadm trigger --subsystem-match=input --attr-match=idVendor=054c --attr-match=idProduct=0ce6
#
# ==============================================================================
# Manual Calibration (one-time, not persistent)
# ==============================================================================
#
# To test different deadzone values temporarily:
#
#   evdev-joystick --evdev /dev/input/by-id/usb-Sony_*-event-joystick --axis 0 --deadzone 2000
#
# To make permanent changes, edit modules/gaming/gaming.nix udev rules.
#
# ==============================================================================
